      "label": "8",
      "prompt": "$5x^2+px-8=q(x-1)^2+r$. Find $p,q,r$.",
      "answerSpaceMm": 28,
      "answer": {
        "short": "$p=-10,\\ q=5,\\ r=-13$",
        "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5x^2+px-8&=q(x^2-2x+1)+r\\\\5x^2+px-8&=qx^2-2qx+q+r\\end{align*}$$\nEquate coefficients and constant terms.\n$$\\begin{align*}q&=5\\\\p&=-2(5)=-10\\\\-8&=5+r\\\\r&=-13\\end{align*}$$",
